{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Contracted Ideal.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Contracted Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"contracted ideal contracted ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Contracted Ideal.md","fileName":"Contracted Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Contracted Ideal","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Localization and Local Algebra]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Localization and Local Algebra","Ring Homomorphism","Ring Localization","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Contracted Ideal.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Contracted Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"contracted ideal contracted ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Contracted Ideal.md","fileName":"Contracted Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Contracted Ideal","heading":"Contracted Ideal","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Given a [[Ring Homomorphism]] f: R → T and an ideal J of T, the contracted ideal Jᶜ is the inverse image f⁻¹(J) in R. It contains exactly the source elements whose images lie in J.\n\nFor [[Ring Localization]], every ideal of the localized ring is the extension of its contraction. Prime ideals of the localization correspond to source primes disjoint from the denominator set.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Localization and Local Algebra","Ring Homomorphism","Ring Localization","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Contracted Ideal.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Contracted Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"contracted ideal contracted ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Contracted Ideal.md","fileName":"Contracted Ideal.md","folder":"6 - F